1
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:39,328
It started when I was a baby.

2
00:01:40,168 --> 00:01:41,608
That's when I first saw it.

3
00:01:42,308 --> 00:01:43,908
Shogi's been with me ever since.

4
00:01:46,968 --> 00:01:48,768
I grew up in the northeast.

5
00:01:49,408 --> 00:01:51,648
My village had snow and not much else.

6
00:01:52,348 --> 00:01:55,308
There were more cows and roosters than people living there.

7
00:01:55,968 --> 00:01:58,628
And of those people, most were senior citizens.

8
00:01:58,628 --> 00:02:02,168
There weren't many other children my own age to play with.

9
00:02:02,608 --> 00:02:05,448
Not even enough to play baseball or soccer.

10
00:02:06,168 --> 00:02:07,608
That's where I grew up.

11
00:02:09,208 --> 00:02:10,728
There wasn't much to do.

12
00:02:11,268 --> 00:02:16,248
I could catch bugs by myself, or play video games, or read.

13
00:02:17,148 --> 00:02:19,928
Then one day, as I sat alone by the heater,

14
00:02:20,928 --> 00:02:26,028
a few old men from the neighborhood decided to teach me how to play shogi.

15
00:02:26,028 --> 00:02:29,748
This piece here is the king.

16
00:02:30,268 --> 00:02:31,608
That's the gold general.

17
00:02:32,608 --> 00:02:35,428
Rook, bishop, and silver.

18
00:02:37,748 --> 00:02:40,108
For games, manga, and novels,

19
00:02:40,868 --> 00:02:42,488
the end always came too quickly.

20
00:02:43,408 --> 00:02:44,848
Shogi was different.

21
00:02:45,868 --> 00:02:47,068
There was no end to it.

22
00:02:47,408 --> 00:02:48,968
I just kept going.

23
00:02:49,728 --> 00:02:50,548
I was hooked.

24
00:02:51,088 --> 00:02:53,028
I thought about nothing else after that.

25
00:02:53,028 --> 00:02:53,988
No!

26
00:02:55,568 --> 00:02:57,828
I can't believe that I lost again!

27
00:02:57,848 --> 00:03:01,048
By second grade, I was beating all of the adults in the village.

28
00:03:01,668 --> 00:03:02,868
And by the third grade,

29
00:03:03,468 --> 00:03:07,728
I was taking the bus to study at a small shogi training hall in the city.

30
00:03:09,168 --> 00:03:12,108
Even there, I continued to rise in the ranks.

31
00:03:12,488 --> 00:03:14,228
Oh, great job!

32
00:03:14,508 --> 00:03:15,868
You're amazing, kiddo!

33
00:03:15,868 --> 00:03:22,108
My teacher from the training hall introduced me to Mr. Ouchi.

34
00:03:22,788 --> 00:03:25,708
Under him, I joined the association in Tokyo.

35
00:03:27,448 --> 00:03:31,768
For a middle schooler like me, Tokyo was a faraway place.

36
00:03:31,768 --> 00:03:37,628
I had to take odd jobs around town to pay for transportation.

37
00:03:38,468 --> 00:03:40,908
I'd pick apples and peaches in the summer

38
00:03:40,908 --> 00:03:44,648
and help harvest rice in the fall.

39
00:03:47,208 --> 00:03:48,608
And in the wintertime,

40
00:03:49,228 --> 00:03:51,388
I worked hard taking care of the cattle.

41
00:03:52,668 --> 00:03:54,008
Isn't Kai incredible?

42
00:03:54,468 --> 00:03:56,068
He'll be famous one day.

43
00:03:56,288 --> 00:03:56,948
Wait and see.

44
00:03:57,068 --> 00:03:59,528
This young man might be the village's first magey.

45
00:03:59,528 --> 00:04:03,848
The old men of the village were behind me 100%.

46
00:04:03,848 --> 00:04:09,508
Thanks to my hard-won wages

47
00:04:09,508 --> 00:04:11,888
and the encouragement of the old men

48
00:04:11,888 --> 00:04:13,528
and the local shogi club members,

49
00:04:13,988 --> 00:04:16,408
I continued going to the association

50
00:04:16,408 --> 00:04:18,808
on that bumpy overnight bus.

51
00:04:21,988 --> 00:04:23,488
That's when it began.

52
00:04:24,228 --> 00:04:26,908
I've had issues with my stomach ever since.

53
00:04:29,528 --> 00:04:33,608
It was just like everyone said.

54
00:04:33,928 --> 00:04:36,848
The third den league was a den of wolves.

55
00:04:37,808 --> 00:04:39,608
I was stuck there for years,

56
00:04:40,008 --> 00:04:41,148
unable to advance.

57
00:04:42,028 --> 00:04:44,468
I may have been hailed as a genius back home,

58
00:04:45,148 --> 00:04:45,888
but in the city,

59
00:04:46,308 --> 00:04:49,148
I was just one more brat with a shogi board.

60
00:04:49,148 --> 00:04:54,268
In spite of my complete lack of progress,

61
00:04:55,208 --> 00:04:58,028
the old men of the village never stopped believing in me.

62
00:05:00,428 --> 00:05:03,748
Commuting on the bus overnight felt endless,

63
00:05:04,508 --> 00:05:07,408
my seat squeaking and creaking all the while.

64
00:05:07,408 --> 00:05:12,248
Eventually, it was difficult to know

65
00:05:12,248 --> 00:05:14,368
whether all that noise was coming from the seat,

66
00:05:15,248 --> 00:05:15,928
my stomach,

67
00:05:16,388 --> 00:05:18,468
or if it was all in my head.

68
00:05:18,468 --> 00:05:21,608
I would have awful nightmares

69
00:05:21,608 --> 00:05:23,688
of riding on and on,

70
00:05:24,028 --> 00:05:25,128
never getting anywhere.

71
00:05:26,088 --> 00:05:26,468
Still,

72
00:05:26,788 --> 00:05:28,828
I couldn't let everyone's faith in me

73
00:05:28,828 --> 00:05:30,548
just go to waste.

74
00:05:32,708 --> 00:05:34,468
I didn't want that.

75
00:05:35,868 --> 00:05:37,608
Maybe that's the reason

76
00:05:37,608 --> 00:05:39,528
why this pain

77
00:05:39,528 --> 00:05:43,548
has me in its grips.

78
00:05:43,548 --> 00:05:47,388
Excuse me.

79
00:05:49,228 --> 00:05:50,508
Hey there, Kiriyama.

80
00:05:51,128 --> 00:05:52,168
Oh, it's okay.

81
00:05:52,368 --> 00:05:53,128
You don't have to get up.

82
00:05:53,648 --> 00:05:54,768
I got you a few groceries.

83
00:05:55,168 --> 00:05:56,448
I'll just put them in the fridge for you.

84
00:05:57,468 --> 00:05:58,308
Thanks a lot.

85
00:05:58,608 --> 00:05:59,368
It's nothing.

86
00:06:00,248 --> 00:06:01,568
I'm on spring break now.

87
00:06:02,288 --> 00:06:03,408
Have you had lunch yet?

88
00:06:04,568 --> 00:06:05,008
No,

89
00:06:05,368 --> 00:06:07,088
just tofu and a little something.

90
00:06:07,968 --> 00:06:09,848
I can make you some noodles if you'd like.

91
00:06:11,188 --> 00:06:12,628
They're pretty easy on the stomach

92
00:06:12,628 --> 00:06:13,568
if you make them soft.

93
00:06:14,228 --> 00:06:14,548
Oh,

94
00:06:14,788 --> 00:06:15,728
in that case,

95
00:06:15,768 --> 00:06:16,908
I might be able to have some.

96
00:06:17,368 --> 00:06:17,808
Thanks.

97
00:06:18,348 --> 00:06:19,728
My dad had stomach aches too,

98
00:06:20,328 --> 00:06:21,568
so I know how that can be.

99
00:06:22,228 --> 00:06:23,548
It'll just take a few minutes.

100
00:06:24,528 --> 00:06:25,288
He did?

101
00:06:25,548 --> 00:06:28,108
I didn't know that Mr. Kota had stomach aches.

102
00:06:30,668 --> 00:06:32,208
Do you mind if I add an egg?

103
00:06:37,248 --> 00:06:38,128
Not him.

104
00:06:38,868 --> 00:06:39,768
Yeah, sure.

105
00:06:40,708 --> 00:06:41,188
Please.

106
00:06:42,628 --> 00:06:43,588
I see.

107
00:06:43,588 --> 00:06:46,148
He meant his real father.

108
00:06:51,748 --> 00:06:52,948
It looks good.

109
00:06:55,948 --> 00:06:56,888
Not bad.

110
00:06:57,228 --> 00:06:58,628
I think this will be fine.

111
00:06:58,968 --> 00:06:59,348
Thanks.

112
00:06:59,988 --> 00:07:00,608
That's great.

113
00:07:00,788 --> 00:07:01,028
Good.

114
00:07:01,968 --> 00:07:02,448
Well then,

115
00:07:02,688 --> 00:07:03,448
if you don't mind,

116
00:07:03,788 --> 00:07:05,248
I guess I should be heading home now.

117
00:07:06,008 --> 00:07:06,348
Oh,

118
00:07:06,488 --> 00:07:07,368
do you have to go?

119
00:07:07,368 --> 00:07:09,848
Your fourth match is in five days,

120
00:07:10,048 --> 00:07:10,908
so right now,

121
00:07:11,108 --> 00:07:12,528
you need to focus on getting better

122
00:07:12,528 --> 00:07:13,668
so you'll be ready for it.

123
00:07:13,868 --> 00:07:15,388
It's important you don't overdo it.

124
00:07:16,828 --> 00:07:17,308
Yeah,

125
00:07:17,368 --> 00:07:18,488
I think I'll be all right.

126
00:07:18,888 --> 00:07:20,968
These stomach pains are nothing new to me.

127
00:07:21,648 --> 00:07:23,748
It's never really a problem during a match.

128
00:07:24,388 --> 00:07:24,868
Uh,

129
00:07:25,108 --> 00:07:26,348
you sure about that?

130
00:07:27,748 --> 00:07:28,228
Yeah,

131
00:07:28,568 --> 00:07:29,828
but with that being said,

132
00:07:29,888 --> 00:07:30,228
however,

133
00:07:30,228 --> 00:07:32,148
I found myself in a pinch.

134
00:07:33,108 --> 00:07:35,668
I don't usually like to make any sealed moves,

135
00:07:36,188 --> 00:07:37,648
but I had to this time.

136
00:07:38,128 --> 00:07:40,128
During the natural flow of the game,

137
00:07:40,268 --> 00:07:41,888
I came up with a really good move.

138
00:07:42,308 --> 00:07:43,468
That's how I decided

139
00:07:43,468 --> 00:07:45,328
on my sealed move.

140
00:07:45,488 --> 00:07:46,228
But later that night...

141
00:07:46,228 --> 00:07:48,628
Four-sixth bishop?

142
00:07:48,748 --> 00:07:49,688
Not six-sixth silver!

143
00:07:49,828 --> 00:07:50,508
Silver's same!

144
00:07:50,968 --> 00:07:51,788
The six-five pawn

145
00:07:51,788 --> 00:07:52,648
then takes that silver.

146
00:07:52,768 --> 00:07:53,488
Rook at five-five

147
00:07:53,488 --> 00:07:54,428
takes six-six lance,

148
00:07:54,528 --> 00:07:56,188
but I overlooked that four-sixth bishop!

149
00:07:56,348 --> 00:07:57,428
I'm a goner!

150
00:07:58,148 --> 00:07:58,588
No!

151
00:07:59,008 --> 00:08:00,248
You'll have me checkmated

152
00:08:00,248 --> 00:08:01,248
before lunch!

153
00:08:01,548 --> 00:08:02,308
By then,

154
00:08:02,388 --> 00:08:03,228
it was too late.

155
00:08:03,948 --> 00:08:04,968
Much too late.

156
00:08:05,368 --> 00:08:07,108
So I spent the whole night

157
00:08:07,108 --> 00:08:08,108
trying to think of a way

158
00:08:08,108 --> 00:08:09,308
I could stay in the game.

159
00:08:09,668 --> 00:08:11,428
And my stomach was on fire.

160
00:08:11,848 --> 00:08:13,108
I tossed and turned

161
00:08:13,108 --> 00:08:14,728
endlessly until morning.

162
00:08:16,228 --> 00:08:19,768
Wait, what was it

163
00:08:19,768 --> 00:08:21,408
that I was talking about again?

164
00:08:21,528 --> 00:08:21,768
See?

165
00:08:21,968 --> 00:08:23,088
This is exactly why

166
00:08:23,088 --> 00:08:23,628
I'm telling you

167
00:08:23,628 --> 00:08:24,508
that you need to rest.

168
00:08:25,728 --> 00:08:26,508
Yeah, yeah.

169
00:08:26,628 --> 00:08:27,208
All right.

170
00:08:28,428 --> 00:08:30,388
Anyway, shall we?

171
00:08:30,908 --> 00:08:32,568
I'll go with a static rook

172
00:08:32,568 --> 00:08:34,488
and you go with a ranging rook, okay?

173
00:08:35,008 --> 00:08:36,848
You're not listening to me, are you?

174
00:08:42,848 --> 00:08:45,448
Are you sure about this?

175
00:08:45,448 --> 00:08:46,948
Is it even useful

176
00:08:46,948 --> 00:08:47,768
for you to be playing

177
00:08:47,768 --> 00:08:48,848
against someone like me?

178
00:08:49,468 --> 00:08:50,488
Am I the only one

179
00:08:50,488 --> 00:08:51,708
who's benefiting from this?

180
00:08:52,408 --> 00:08:53,128
After all,

181
00:08:53,248 --> 00:08:54,088
I'm only C1

182
00:08:54,088 --> 00:08:54,988
and you're A-class,

183
00:08:55,128 --> 00:08:56,148
so there's a lot I can learn

184
00:08:56,148 --> 00:08:57,668
by playing against someone like you.

185
00:08:58,488 --> 00:08:59,308
But how

186
00:08:59,308 --> 00:09:00,828
does it help you out

187
00:09:00,828 --> 00:09:01,908
by playing against me?

188
00:09:01,908 --> 00:09:05,788
Well, the thing is,

189
00:09:06,128 --> 00:09:07,828
sometimes you sound like him.

190
00:09:08,228 --> 00:09:09,728
It's how you phrase things.

191
00:09:09,948 --> 00:09:10,168
Huh?

192
00:09:11,168 --> 00:09:12,028
You remember?

193
00:09:12,848 --> 00:09:14,528
You said it's unsettling.

194
00:09:15,148 --> 00:09:15,608
Um,

195
00:09:16,068 --> 00:09:17,508
how can I put this?

196
00:09:18,188 --> 00:09:19,448
It just feels like it's

197
00:09:20,108 --> 00:09:20,808
unsettling.

198
00:09:20,808 --> 00:09:24,748
When Soya saw Silver to 3-7,

199
00:09:25,228 --> 00:09:26,368
he said that too.

200
00:09:26,588 --> 00:09:27,928
He was sitting in the waiting room

201
00:09:27,928 --> 00:09:28,688
just talking.

202
00:09:29,748 --> 00:09:32,068
That Silver to 3-7 move

203
00:09:32,068 --> 00:09:33,048
was unsettling.

204
00:09:33,048 --> 00:09:34,928
You know,

205
00:09:35,648 --> 00:09:37,408
you two are kind of similar.

206
00:09:38,168 --> 00:09:39,988
Not in any particular way.

207
00:09:40,648 --> 00:09:41,908
But you both see the game

208
00:09:41,908 --> 00:09:43,148
in a similar fashion,

209
00:09:43,448 --> 00:09:44,948
and of course you're all-rounders

210
00:09:44,948 --> 00:09:45,848
in your own right.

211
00:09:46,588 --> 00:09:47,768
You're both very good

212
00:09:47,768 --> 00:09:49,068
at offense and defense,

213
00:09:49,408 --> 00:09:50,948
as well as your sense of timing

214
00:09:50,948 --> 00:09:52,248
when you're making a decision.

215
00:09:53,048 --> 00:09:55,148
So when you're sitting across from me,

216
00:09:55,328 --> 00:09:56,288
playing as you do,

217
00:09:56,288 --> 00:09:58,488
I feel like I can figure out

218
00:09:58,488 --> 00:10:00,808
a tiny bit of Soya's thought process.

219
00:10:01,768 --> 00:10:03,388
It's probably just temporary,

220
00:10:03,848 --> 00:10:04,668
but it's better than

221
00:10:04,668 --> 00:10:05,948
not practicing at all.

222
00:10:09,368 --> 00:10:11,308
So tell me what Grand Master Soya

223
00:10:11,308 --> 00:10:12,428
is really like in person.

224
00:10:13,048 --> 00:10:13,288
Huh?

225
00:10:13,648 --> 00:10:14,468
That's right.

226
00:10:14,828 --> 00:10:15,848
Now that you mention it,

227
00:10:16,308 --> 00:10:17,308
I guess when you've got

228
00:10:17,308 --> 00:10:18,168
that many titles,

229
00:10:18,548 --> 00:10:19,668
you don't really make your way

230
00:10:19,668 --> 00:10:21,108
to Shogi Hall too often.

231
00:10:21,668 --> 00:10:23,368
He probably just shows up

232
00:10:23,368 --> 00:10:24,448
to sign certificates.

233
00:10:24,448 --> 00:10:27,208
Let me see.

234
00:10:27,368 --> 00:10:28,408
How do I put this?

235
00:10:29,568 --> 00:10:31,188
He reminds me of a bird.

236
00:10:31,868 --> 00:10:32,388
A bird?

237
00:10:33,028 --> 00:10:33,528
Yeah.

238
00:10:34,168 --> 00:10:35,768
Quiet and gentle,

239
00:10:36,088 --> 00:10:38,088
like an egret or a crane.

240
00:10:38,608 --> 00:10:39,468
It's sort of like

241
00:10:39,468 --> 00:10:41,688
the story of the tortoise and the hare,

242
00:10:42,888 --> 00:10:44,568
except he's much higher up

243
00:10:44,568 --> 00:10:45,848
and seems to have

244
00:10:45,848 --> 00:10:47,108
the presence of a bird.

245
00:10:48,448 --> 00:10:49,868
Whenever I see Soya,

246
00:10:50,368 --> 00:10:52,188
I pretty much feel like the tortoise

247
00:10:52,188 --> 00:10:53,768
crawling along the ground.

248
00:10:54,448 --> 00:10:55,968
And I don't mean that

249
00:10:55,968 --> 00:10:56,808
in a bad way.

250
00:10:57,208 --> 00:10:57,848
Not at all.

251
00:10:58,888 --> 00:11:00,528
What continues to puzzle me

252
00:11:00,528 --> 00:11:02,168
is that the hare's laziness

253
00:11:02,168 --> 00:11:03,528
is caused by overconfidence.

254
00:11:04,748 --> 00:11:05,948
But with Soya,

255
00:11:06,428 --> 00:11:07,488
as you might expect

256
00:11:07,488 --> 00:11:08,928
from someone labeled a genius,

257
00:11:09,448 --> 00:11:11,228
he doesn't ever slack off.

258
00:11:12,228 --> 00:11:14,008
No matter how high he climbs,

259
00:11:14,108 --> 00:11:15,068
he never rests

260
00:11:15,068 --> 00:11:17,348
and always maintains his confidence,

261
00:11:17,348 --> 00:11:20,608
which is why I can never catch up to him,

262
00:11:20,608 --> 00:11:22,368
no matter what I do.

263
00:11:23,628 --> 00:11:26,068
I've been watching him all this time.

264
00:11:26,768 --> 00:11:28,128
We're both the same age,

265
00:11:28,268 --> 00:11:29,828
but he blew through the association

266
00:11:29,828 --> 00:11:31,288
like a gust of wind.

267
00:11:32,028 --> 00:11:33,288
I watched him go pro

268
00:11:33,288 --> 00:11:35,608
and make quick work of the competition.

269
00:11:35,608 --> 00:11:40,708
Just because there's distance between us

270
00:11:40,708 --> 00:11:42,748
doesn't mean I should stop trying

271
00:11:42,748 --> 00:11:43,648
to move forward.

272
00:11:44,648 --> 00:11:46,188
Just because it's obvious

273
00:11:46,188 --> 00:11:47,588
that I can't get ahead of him

274
00:11:47,588 --> 00:11:51,248
is no excuse for not making the effort.

275
00:11:51,248 --> 00:11:54,708
Mr. Shimada,

276
00:11:54,868 --> 00:11:55,928
are you okay?

277
00:11:56,108 --> 00:11:57,588
I think you need to see a doctor.

278
00:11:57,928 --> 00:11:59,628
No, I'm fine, really.

279
00:12:00,008 --> 00:12:01,288
I already saw one.

280
00:12:01,368 --> 00:12:02,568
But Mr. Shimada...

281
00:12:02,568 --> 00:12:05,048
I've got plenty of medicine, too.

282
00:12:05,768 --> 00:12:07,148
I've been living with this pain

283
00:12:07,148 --> 00:12:08,088
since my teens.

284
00:12:08,668 --> 00:12:10,688
It's just part of my life now.

285
00:12:12,908 --> 00:12:14,728
It does get old, though.

286
00:12:15,188 --> 00:12:17,348
If only my stomach were a bit stronger.

287
00:12:18,048 --> 00:12:19,228
Sorry, Kiriyama,

288
00:12:19,388 --> 00:12:20,468
could you get me some water?

289
00:12:20,468 --> 00:12:21,888
Oh, uh, yeah.

290
00:12:22,808 --> 00:12:24,808
Sorry for asking you to come over here

291
00:12:24,808 --> 00:12:26,268
when I'm not feeling so well.

292
00:12:26,508 --> 00:12:26,948
I know.

293
00:12:27,068 --> 00:12:27,548
Don't worry.

294
00:12:29,248 --> 00:12:30,848
I really don't mind at all.

295
00:12:34,928 --> 00:12:37,048
All right, then.

296
00:12:37,988 --> 00:12:39,448
Would you mind sticking around?

297
00:12:39,628 --> 00:12:40,348
A bit longer.

298
00:12:40,948 --> 00:12:43,048
I won the right to challenge Soya.

299
00:12:44,008 --> 00:12:46,328
So I can't let him win without a fight.

300
00:12:46,808 --> 00:12:47,988
I've got to keep trying.

301
00:12:47,988 --> 00:12:50,828
That's all that matters.

302
00:12:52,328 --> 00:12:53,148
After all,

303
00:12:53,368 --> 00:12:54,968
they still have the banner there.

304
00:12:55,528 --> 00:12:57,208
It's in my local train station,

305
00:12:57,588 --> 00:12:58,408
plain as day.

306
00:12:59,148 --> 00:13:00,048
You know what's worse?

307
00:13:00,048 --> 00:13:02,388
I'm the only one.

308
00:13:02,388 --> 00:13:05,108
Nobody has ever made it this far.

309
00:13:05,848 --> 00:13:08,748
I'm Yamagata's only highly ranked player.

310
00:13:09,848 --> 00:13:13,008
That's why I have to do this.

311
00:13:13,808 --> 00:13:14,668
No matter what,

312
00:13:15,088 --> 00:13:16,868
I can't ignore that banner.

313
00:13:17,768 --> 00:13:19,628
A lot of people are depending on me,

314
00:13:20,008 --> 00:13:21,808
and I can't let them down.

315
00:13:21,808 --> 00:13:22,808
There.

316
00:13:39,148 --> 00:13:41,288
This train will be departing at 8.05.

317
00:13:41,968 --> 00:13:43,128
I brought you a blanket.

318
00:13:44,348 --> 00:13:46,188
And if you'd like to have some tea,

319
00:13:46,588 --> 00:13:48,428
I'll put one here in the seat pocket for you.

320
00:13:48,968 --> 00:13:51,408
Thanks for going to all this trouble.

321
00:13:54,268 --> 00:13:56,048
The trip takes about two hours.

322
00:13:56,588 --> 00:13:57,828
I'll wake you up when we get there.

323
00:13:58,128 --> 00:13:58,948
So try to sleep.

324
00:13:59,128 --> 00:13:59,408
Okay.

325
00:14:00,308 --> 00:14:02,028
Thanks for everything, really.

326
00:14:03,108 --> 00:14:04,028
No problem.

327
00:14:04,028 --> 00:14:07,368
Later that night...

328
00:14:07,368 --> 00:14:09,588
One more loss and the next is do or die.

329
00:14:10,028 --> 00:14:11,288
All straight losses.

330
00:14:11,708 --> 00:14:12,788
Can't let that happen.

331
00:14:14,168 --> 00:14:16,368
He urged me to continue practicing with him,

332
00:14:17,008 --> 00:14:18,708
even though he was still in great pain.

333
00:14:21,488 --> 00:14:22,548
I'll be here for you.

334
00:14:22,608 --> 00:14:23,288
It's no problem.

335
00:14:23,628 --> 00:14:25,268
But I just can't let you travel alone.

336
00:14:25,808 --> 00:14:26,628
Thanks a lot.

337
00:14:26,628 --> 00:14:28,888
However,

338
00:14:29,748 --> 00:14:31,688
as I watched Mr. Shimada sleep,

339
00:14:32,288 --> 00:14:34,708
a strong sense of regret surged through me.

340
00:14:35,528 --> 00:14:37,308
I never should have let it get this far.

341
00:14:37,848 --> 00:14:39,508
I should have made him take a break.

342
00:14:40,708 --> 00:14:42,488
We've now arrived in Kyoto.

343
00:14:42,968 --> 00:14:45,228
Please remember to take all of your belongings.

344
00:14:47,468 --> 00:14:49,508
Alright, so where do we find a taxi?

345
00:14:50,328 --> 00:14:51,268
On the right,

346
00:14:51,488 --> 00:14:52,668
facing Kyoto Tower.

347
00:14:52,668 --> 00:14:54,288
Oh, right.

348
00:14:55,288 --> 00:14:57,628
Take us to the second Kyoto Hotel, please.

349
00:14:57,868 --> 00:14:58,288
Sure.

350
00:15:13,288 --> 00:15:14,208
There he is!

351
00:15:14,868 --> 00:15:15,928
Hey, Shimada!

352
00:15:18,028 --> 00:15:18,508
Kiriyama!

353
00:15:18,728 --> 00:15:19,868
Glad you could make it, too!

354
00:15:20,388 --> 00:15:21,608
So sorry, Chairman.

355
00:15:21,608 --> 00:15:23,208
We didn't mean to make you worry.

356
00:15:23,428 --> 00:15:24,728
It's your stomach again, huh?

357
00:15:24,948 --> 00:15:26,708
Man, you've always been so sickly.

358
00:15:27,108 --> 00:15:27,508
Right?

359
00:15:29,708 --> 00:15:30,108
Sorry.

360
00:15:30,748 --> 00:15:32,468
Can't they just do a stomach transplant?

361
00:15:33,028 --> 00:15:33,688
At this rate,

362
00:15:33,728 --> 00:15:35,068
you'll never be able to win a title.

363
00:15:35,808 --> 00:15:36,408
Sure, man!

364
00:15:36,428 --> 00:15:37,768
You're just making things worse!

365
00:15:38,028 --> 00:15:38,888
Well, never mind.

366
00:15:38,988 --> 00:15:40,508
Go and get some rest until the reception.

367
00:15:40,988 --> 00:15:41,268
Hey!

368
00:15:41,368 --> 00:15:42,328
Can I get the bellboy?

369
00:15:43,608 --> 00:15:49,168
I'll come by once you get some rest.

370
00:15:49,168 --> 00:15:53,528
I put your phone and some water and tea next to your pillow.

371
00:15:54,128 --> 00:15:56,168
Just give me a call if you need anything else.

372
00:15:58,768 --> 00:16:01,248
You kind of sound like my mom.

373
00:16:01,848 --> 00:16:02,288
Sorry!

374
00:16:02,508 --> 00:16:02,968
My bad!

375
00:16:03,188 --> 00:16:04,268
Am I being too pushy?

376
00:16:04,448 --> 00:16:05,628
No, no, you're fine.

377
00:16:05,768 --> 00:16:06,328
Don't worry.

378
00:16:08,628 --> 00:16:09,988
Thanks for helping out.

379
00:16:09,988 --> 00:16:17,508
So far, so good.

380
00:16:17,968 --> 00:16:19,488
I wonder what I should do next.

381
00:16:20,488 --> 00:16:21,048
Hmm.

382
00:16:21,888 --> 00:16:22,588
I know.

383
00:16:22,988 --> 00:16:24,108
I'll go pick up a book,

384
00:16:24,288 --> 00:16:25,708
and maybe I'll get something to drink.

385
00:16:26,328 --> 00:16:26,968
You know,

386
00:16:27,248 --> 00:16:28,948
you surprise me, Kiriyama.

387
00:16:29,348 --> 00:16:32,068
I always thought you were a pretty cold and distant kid,

388
00:16:32,168 --> 00:16:33,308
but I guess I was wrong.

389
00:16:35,468 --> 00:16:36,948
It's been a huge help,

390
00:16:37,028 --> 00:16:38,248
you bringing Shimada here.

391
00:16:39,828 --> 00:16:41,288
Well, I gotta get going.

392
00:16:41,428 --> 00:16:43,008
I've gotta go and find Soya.

393
00:16:43,428 --> 00:16:44,868
He still hasn't shown up yet.

394
00:16:45,008 --> 00:16:46,068
Since he lives close by,

395
00:16:46,128 --> 00:16:48,008
he always waits to leave home at the last minute.

396
00:16:48,228 --> 00:16:49,068
He lives here?

397
00:16:49,628 --> 00:16:50,288
Yeah, sure.

398
00:16:50,428 --> 00:16:51,468
By the Silver Pavilion.

399
00:16:51,908 --> 00:16:53,088
That place is incredible.

400
00:16:53,688 --> 00:16:55,288
Don't all the tourists get annoying?

401
00:16:55,708 --> 00:16:56,328
Not really.

402
00:16:56,548 --> 00:16:57,908
It's actually pretty quiet there.

403
00:16:58,668 --> 00:17:00,688
Is there anyone at his place you could call?

404
00:17:01,268 --> 00:17:02,568
Nobody ever picks up.

405
00:17:03,828 --> 00:17:04,268
You see,

406
00:17:04,528 --> 00:17:06,208
he's living with his grandmother now,

407
00:17:06,408 --> 00:17:08,168
and she's gotten a bit hard of hearing,

408
00:17:08,368 --> 00:17:08,908
so...

409
00:17:08,908 --> 00:17:11,088
I'm gonna go over there

410
00:17:11,088 --> 00:17:12,248
and find out for myself.

411
00:17:22,128 --> 00:17:24,148
So I'm back in Kyoto.

412
00:17:24,148 --> 00:17:27,088
I haven't been here since I was in middle school.

413
00:17:28,368 --> 00:17:30,368
Maybe I should pick up some souvenirs.

414
00:17:31,028 --> 00:17:32,848
I wonder what Hina and the girls would like.

415
00:17:32,848 --> 00:17:39,408
Hey, where's Kiriyama?

416
00:17:39,408 --> 00:17:40,108
I don't know.

417
00:17:40,388 --> 00:17:40,908
Who cares?

418
00:17:41,008 --> 00:17:41,968
It's free time, right?

419
00:17:42,808 --> 00:17:44,288
He can do whatever he wants.

420
00:17:44,688 --> 00:17:45,348
Good point.

421
00:17:45,348 --> 00:17:51,308
Guess I'll just head back.

422
00:17:51,308 --> 00:17:53,648
There's nothing I really want to see here.

423
00:17:55,648 --> 00:17:59,148
The pre-match reception for the fourth game of the Shishio Tournament

424
00:17:59,148 --> 00:18:00,368
was held that night.

425
00:18:00,728 --> 00:18:02,088
It was a grand gala.

426
00:18:03,088 --> 00:18:05,088
Mr. Shimada was surrounded by the press.

427
00:18:05,508 --> 00:18:07,048
He humbly responded with a smile,

428
00:18:07,348 --> 00:18:08,328
answering their questions.

429
00:18:08,328 --> 00:18:09,428
However,

430
00:18:09,948 --> 00:18:12,168
he hadn't eaten anything since the night before,

431
00:18:12,668 --> 00:18:14,968
and he was still in pain just a little while ago.

432
00:18:16,588 --> 00:18:17,968
You can't do this.

433
00:18:18,148 --> 00:18:19,488
If it keeps up till tomorrow,

434
00:18:19,588 --> 00:18:20,448
you'll lose everything.

435
00:18:21,108 --> 00:18:21,568
Yeah,

436
00:18:21,808 --> 00:18:24,488
I'm painfully aware of the situation.

437
00:18:24,488 --> 00:18:30,488
My most important job is giving everyone a good match.

438
00:18:31,288 --> 00:18:33,908
It's also very important that I stand tall

439
00:18:33,908 --> 00:18:35,528
before the people who were kind enough

440
00:18:35,528 --> 00:18:37,448
to organize this event for us.

441
00:18:39,448 --> 00:18:41,048
I understand that,

442
00:18:41,348 --> 00:18:42,488
but still...

443
00:18:43,788 --> 00:18:46,948
It hurt to watch as the cameras flashed at him.

444
00:18:47,968 --> 00:18:49,488
Mr. Shimada...

445
00:18:49,488 --> 00:18:52,168
I had the feeling that each flash

446
00:18:52,168 --> 00:18:55,528
caused a burning sensation in Mr. Shimada's gut.

447
00:18:57,628 --> 00:18:59,308
They're talking to each other.

448
00:19:07,868 --> 00:19:08,988
Mr. Shimada?

449
00:19:09,888 --> 00:19:10,908
I'm leaving,

450
00:19:11,308 --> 00:19:11,988
stealthily.

451
00:19:12,628 --> 00:19:13,608
So suddenly?

452
00:19:14,008 --> 00:19:14,688
Are you okay?

453
00:19:15,128 --> 00:19:15,908
Don't worry.

454
00:19:16,168 --> 00:19:17,908
I did everything I had to do.

455
00:19:19,468 --> 00:19:21,248
He wanted to help me out.

456
00:19:21,248 --> 00:19:23,648
So I'll leave the rest to him.

457
00:19:26,848 --> 00:19:27,328
Hey,

458
00:19:27,668 --> 00:19:28,988
good job working the crowd.

459
00:19:29,328 --> 00:19:30,568
Sorry for leaving early.

460
00:19:30,748 --> 00:19:31,868
I need to get some rest.

461
00:19:32,008 --> 00:19:32,228
Aw,

462
00:19:32,288 --> 00:19:33,468
that's not a problem at all.

463
00:19:33,548 --> 00:19:33,828
Really,

464
00:19:33,988 --> 00:19:35,028
no one will even notice,

465
00:19:35,148 --> 00:19:35,648
I'm sure.

466
00:19:35,968 --> 00:19:36,268
Besides,

467
00:19:36,588 --> 00:19:37,988
everyone's here to see...

468
00:19:37,988 --> 00:19:38,528
Soya!

469
00:19:39,528 --> 00:19:39,988
Understand?

470
00:19:40,388 --> 00:19:41,808
So go ahead and get some rest!

471
00:19:42,148 --> 00:19:42,588
Chairman!

472
00:19:42,588 --> 00:19:45,128
I know, right?

473
00:19:45,508 --> 00:19:47,388
As long as I say hello to everyone,

474
00:19:47,588 --> 00:19:48,348
the rest of the night

475
00:19:48,348 --> 00:19:49,248
pretty much becomes

476
00:19:49,248 --> 00:19:50,668
a Soya photo session.

477
00:19:51,228 --> 00:19:51,528
Yeah,

478
00:19:51,848 --> 00:19:52,928
you've kind of always been

479
00:19:52,928 --> 00:19:54,248
more of the Wallflower type.

480
00:19:54,428 --> 00:19:55,548
You're practically invisible!

481
00:19:55,808 --> 00:19:56,548
Okay, Chairman,

482
00:19:56,728 --> 00:19:57,268
that's enough.

483
00:19:57,388 --> 00:19:58,628
You can stop now, okay?

484
00:19:58,968 --> 00:19:59,248
Really,

485
00:19:59,308 --> 00:20:00,028
you don't need to say

486
00:20:00,028 --> 00:20:01,048
another word, please?

487
00:20:01,388 --> 00:20:03,508
He really does piss me off, though.

488
00:20:03,908 --> 00:20:05,108
Always looking so young

489
00:20:05,108 --> 00:20:05,728
and adorable

490
00:20:05,728 --> 00:20:07,168
with a full head of hair.

491
00:20:07,568 --> 00:20:09,028
Know what the craziest part is?

492
00:20:09,028 --> 00:20:09,848
Your age!

493
00:20:10,008 --> 00:20:11,608
You may be the same age as Soya,

494
00:20:11,708 --> 00:20:12,488
but you look like

495
00:20:12,488 --> 00:20:13,428
you're as old as Goto!

496
00:20:13,988 --> 00:20:15,708
Oh, that's right, Kiriyama.

497
00:20:16,408 --> 00:20:17,308
I meant to tell you

498
00:20:17,308 --> 00:20:18,788
that Smith is going to help you out

499
00:20:18,788 --> 00:20:19,408
with your room,

500
00:20:19,568 --> 00:20:21,328
so go see if you can find him anywhere.

501
00:20:21,788 --> 00:20:24,088
He's here as an assistant observer this year.

502
00:20:24,308 --> 00:20:25,968
Uh, no, that's okay.

503
00:20:26,208 --> 00:20:27,368
I'll go to an internet cafe.

504
00:20:27,748 --> 00:20:28,248
Come on,

505
00:20:28,288 --> 00:20:29,388
I can't let you do that.

506
00:20:29,968 --> 00:20:30,568
Talk to him.

507
00:20:30,828 --> 00:20:32,168
I'm sure Smith won't mind

508
00:20:32,168 --> 00:20:33,368
sharing his room with you.

509
00:20:33,748 --> 00:20:34,668
See you tomorrow.

510
00:20:34,928 --> 00:20:35,368
Good night.

511
00:20:35,848 --> 00:20:36,808
Have a good night!

512
00:20:37,088 --> 00:20:37,488
Bye.

513
00:20:37,488 --> 00:20:39,028
Even when he's in pain,

514
00:20:39,108 --> 00:20:40,468
he still thinks of others.

515
00:20:40,708 --> 00:20:41,548
Poor thing.

516
00:20:41,868 --> 00:20:43,428
It's no wonder his stomach hurts.

517
00:20:46,308 --> 00:20:47,508
What do you want?

518
00:20:47,748 --> 00:20:48,848
I was just about to enjoy

519
00:20:48,848 --> 00:20:49,708
some me time

520
00:20:49,708 --> 00:20:50,708
in this fancy room.

521
00:20:51,528 --> 00:20:52,688
Sorry, I'm fine.

522
00:20:52,848 --> 00:20:54,248
I'll just go to an internet cafe.

523
00:20:54,848 --> 00:20:56,108
I was just kidding.

524
00:20:56,488 --> 00:20:57,208
Take it easy.

525
00:20:57,348 --> 00:20:57,928
What a pain.

526
00:20:58,208 --> 00:20:58,848
Knock it off!

527
00:21:03,768 --> 00:21:04,508
Someone's calling.

528
00:21:04,888 --> 00:21:05,648
Hold on a second.

529
00:21:06,328 --> 00:21:06,748
Hey there,

530
00:21:06,748 --> 00:21:07,568
what's going on?

531
00:21:08,728 --> 00:21:09,508
It's okay.

532
00:21:09,828 --> 00:21:10,408
How about you?

533
00:21:11,208 --> 00:21:12,268
Oh, I was thinking

534
00:21:12,268 --> 00:21:13,168
of calling it a night.

535
00:21:14,168 --> 00:21:14,468
Yeah.

536
00:21:14,928 --> 00:21:15,208
Uh-huh.

537
00:21:16,148 --> 00:21:16,588
Really?

538
00:21:17,308 --> 00:21:18,248
Acting all lonely

539
00:21:18,248 --> 00:21:19,488
without me around, huh?

540
00:21:19,908 --> 00:21:20,328
Uh-huh.

541
00:21:20,948 --> 00:21:21,308
Oh?

542
00:21:21,848 --> 00:21:22,168
Yeah?

543
00:21:22,468 --> 00:21:23,308
A healthy appetite?

544
00:21:24,168 --> 00:21:25,588
Ate every last bite?

545
00:21:26,128 --> 00:21:26,328
Meow.

546
00:21:26,328 --> 00:21:28,848
Hey, wait.

547
00:21:29,108 --> 00:21:29,948
I heard something.

548
00:21:30,288 --> 00:21:31,328
Was that my strawberry?

549
00:21:31,848 --> 00:21:32,248
What?

550
00:21:32,528 --> 00:21:33,168
How could you?

551
00:21:33,228 --> 00:21:34,608
You're purring for someone else!

552
00:21:34,828 --> 00:21:35,048
Huh?

553
00:21:35,248 --> 00:21:35,828
A girlfriend?

554
00:21:36,368 --> 00:21:38,288
And she's with someone else right now?

555
00:21:38,508 --> 00:21:39,448
A love triangle?

556
00:21:39,768 --> 00:21:41,068
Am I supposed to be hearing this?

557
00:21:41,208 --> 00:21:41,408
Huh?

558
00:21:41,548 --> 00:21:41,868
What?

559
00:21:41,868 --> 00:21:42,908
She's on your lap!

560
00:21:43,088 --> 00:21:43,768
No way!

561
00:21:43,888 --> 00:21:44,568
How could she?

562
00:21:44,688 --> 00:21:45,588
She hates when I hold her

563
00:21:45,588 --> 00:21:46,728
and never sits on my lap!

564
00:21:49,408 --> 00:21:49,888
Depressing.

565
00:21:51,088 --> 00:21:53,108
Hey, um, Mr. Smith?

566
00:21:55,628 --> 00:21:56,148
Kiriyama.

567
00:21:56,148 --> 00:21:57,648
I need a drink.

568
00:21:58,208 --> 00:21:59,108
Can I take the key?

569
00:22:00,008 --> 00:22:01,268
Oh, my little kid.

570
00:22:01,288 --> 00:22:02,148
See you later.

571
00:22:04,008 --> 00:22:04,868
And then,

572
00:22:05,568 --> 00:22:06,768
the night turned to dawn

573
00:22:06,768 --> 00:22:07,928
as if nothing happened

574
00:22:07,928 --> 00:22:10,148
and the time was finally here.

575
00:22:10,568 --> 00:22:11,508
The fourth match

576
00:22:11,508 --> 00:22:12,968
of the Shishio Tournament.

577
00:22:14,468 --> 00:22:14,928
All right.

578
00:22:15,108 --> 00:22:16,288
The time is nine o'clock.

579
00:22:16,948 --> 00:22:17,288
Begin.

580
00:22:17,788 --> 00:22:18,628
Defending champion,

581
00:22:18,788 --> 00:22:19,628
if you will, please.

582
00:22:19,968 --> 00:22:20,668
Let's have a good day.

583
00:22:20,668 --> 00:22:21,668
Let's have a good day.

584
00:22:21,668 --> 00:22:26,648
I hope

585
00:22:26,648 --> 00:22:28,568
Mr. Shimada was able

586
00:22:28,568 --> 00:22:29,988
to get some sleep last night.

587
00:22:30,628 --> 00:22:31,948
He looks exhausted.

588
00:22:32,648 --> 00:22:33,668
Is he still having issues

589
00:22:33,668 --> 00:22:34,268
with his stomach?

590
00:22:37,008 --> 00:22:38,348
What should I have done?

591
00:22:39,128 --> 00:22:40,708
Should I have refused to practice?

592
00:22:41,228 --> 00:22:42,288
Forced him to relax?

593
00:22:45,568 --> 00:22:46,628
It's too late

594
00:22:46,628 --> 00:22:48,568
for me to regret

595
00:22:48,568 --> 00:22:49,748
or take anything back

596
00:22:49,748 --> 00:22:50,408
at this point.

597
00:22:51,668 --> 00:22:52,968
The match had begun

598
00:22:52,968 --> 00:22:54,968
and there was no way

599
00:22:54,968 --> 00:22:55,988
of stopping it now.

600
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:35,991
So suddenly? It starts in 10 minutes!

601
00:24:36,231 --> 00:24:37,871
It's gonna be fine, don't worry!

602
00:24:38,371 --> 00:24:42,251
Sorry about that, Nikaido. I was gonna call you sooner, but I haven't had the chance.

603
00:24:42,711 --> 00:24:45,391
I would have flown to him this time if I didn't have a match.

604
00:24:45,751 --> 00:24:49,871
I wore a new Komodo just for the occasion! Let me be on TV!

605
00:24:51,151 --> 00:24:53,991
It's Mr. Shimada's fourth match in the Shishio Tournament.

606
00:24:54,631 --> 00:24:55,831
I'll have to make some more noodles.

607
00:24:56,691 --> 00:24:58,871
Please watch the next March Comes In Like a Lion.

608
00:25:01,011 --> 00:25:14,231
...

609
00:25:16,551 --> 00:25:23,051
...

610
00:25:24,831 --> 00:25:28,691
...

